row(25, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'ISRAEL DWELT IN SHITTIM — THE TABERNACLE\'S TIMBER; THE PEOPLE BEGAN — NOAH\'S VERB; THE SPEC OF EXODUS 34 BEGINS TO RUN. "{H(25, 1, "וישב", "ישראל", "בשטים")}" ("and Israel dwelt in SHITTIM" — one seat; the last camp (33:49 Abel-shittim), Joshua\'s spies sent "from Shittim" (2:1), Micah\'s "from Shittim to Gilgal" (6:5); the name is "ACACIA (shittim) wood" — the tabernacle\'s timber twenty-six times in Exodus and the ark\'s (Deut 10:3); the Sifrei reads "sitting" as subversion on two exemplars measured on the ink — the calf\'s "the people sat to eat and drink" (Exod 32:6) and the brothers\' "they sat to eat bread" (Gen 37:25); computed) → {A(25, 1, "ויתב", "ישראל", "בשטין")} ("and Israel dwelt in Shittin"); "{H(25, 1, "ויחל", "העם", "לזנות", "אל", "בנות", "מואב")}" ("and the people BEGAN to whore after the daughters of Moab" — "and the people began" one seat; the token\'s Torah four are three verbs in one skin: Noah "BEGAN" the vineyard (Gen 9:20), Noah "WAITED" for the dove (8:10), Moses "ENTREATED" after the calf (Exod 32:11), and this; THE SPEC: Exod 34:15-16 "lest... they whore after their gods and sacrifice to their gods and call you and you eat of their sacrifice, and you take of their DAUGHTERS" — 25:1-2 its RUN clause by clause; computed) → {A(25, 1, "ושרי", "עמא", "למטעי", "בתר", "בנת", "מואב")} ("and the people began to STRAY after the daughters of Moab" — the whoring made straying, cut from the shelf\'s bytes). The register: "and he dwelt", "and he began".')
row(25, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'THEY CALLED THE PEOPLE TO THE SACRIFICES OF THEIR GODS — THE FEMININE "THEIR GODS" AT THE SPEC AND THE RUN ALONE. "{H(25, 2, "ותקראן", "לעם", "לזבחי", "אלהיהן")}" ("and THEY (the daughters) called the people to the sacrifices of THEIR gods" — "their gods" in the FEMININE plural stands in the Bible at two seats: Exod 34:16 "their daughters whore after THEIR gods" and this — the spec\'s rare form at the run; the calling and the eating are 34:15\'s "and he calls you and you eat of his sacrifice"; computed) → {A(25, 2, "וקרא", "לעמא", "לדבחי", "טעותהון")} ("and they called the people to the sacrifices of THEIR ERRORS" — the gods made errors, the idol-word, cut from the shelf\'s bytes); "{H(25, 2, "ויאכל", "העם", "וישתחוו", "לאלהיהן")}" ("and the people ATE and BOWED to their gods" — one seat; Exod 34:14\'s "you shall not bow to another god" the bar broken) → {A(25, 2, "ואכל", "עמא", "וסגידו", "לטעותהון")} ("and the people ate and bowed to their errors"). The register: "and they called", "and he ate", "and they bowed".')
row(25, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'ISRAEL YOKED ITSELF TO BAAL-PEOR — THE HEIFER LID\'S WORD PAID; THE LORD\'S ANGER, THE PORTION\'S THIRD. "{H(25, 3, "ויצמד", "ישראל", "לבעל", "פעור")}" ("and Israel YOKED ITSELF to Baal-peor" — the verb\'s three seats in the Bible (25:3, 25:5 "the yoked ones", Ps 106:28 "they yoked themselves to Baal-peor and ate sacrifices of the dead"); its noun is 19:15\'s LID, "tzamid patil", and Rebekah\'s BRACELETS (Gen 24:22) — the Sifrei\'s allusion at the heifer (126:1, sitting 6) is now the ink\'s own: the fastened lid and the fastened people; Baal-peor the god of Balaam\'s third stand (23:28); computed) → {A(25, 3, "ואתחבר", "ישראל", "לבעלא", "פעור")} ("and Israel JOINED ITSELF to Baal-peor" — the yoking made joining); "{H(25, 3, "ויחר", "אף", "יהוה", "בישראל")}" ("and the anger of the LORD burned against Israel" — the portion\'s THIRD anger after God\'s at Balaam\'s going (22:22) and Balak\'s at Balaam (24:10); the clause in the Torah here and Moses\' retelling of this wrath (32:13); computed) → {A(25, 3, "ותקף", "רגזא", "דיי", "בישראל")} ("and the anger of the LORD grew strong against Israel"). The register: "and he yoked himself", "and it burned".')
row(25, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'THE LORD TO MOSES — THE PORTION\'S FIRST WORD TO HIM: HANG THE HEADS BEFORE THE SUN; THE TRANSLATION INSERTS THE COURT. "{H(25, 4, "ויאמר", "יהוה", "אל", "משה")}" ("and the LORD said to Moses" — the FIRST frame to Moses in the portion: chapters 22-24 have none, God speaking nine times to Balaam and his ass; computed) → {A(25, 4, "ואמר", "יי", "למשה")} ("and the LORD said to Moses"); "{H(25, 4, "קח", "את", "כל", "ראשי", "העם", "והוקע", "אותם", "ליהוה", "נגד", "השמש")}" ("take all the heads of the people and HANG them to the LORD BEFORE THE SUN" — "take all the heads" one seat; the hang-verb\'s other seats are Saul\'s seven sons "hanged to the LORD" at Gibeah by the Gibeonites (2 Sam 21:6, 9, 13) — the same verb and the same "to the LORD"; Jacob\'s hip "was WRENCHED" (Gen 32:26) its consonantal kin; "before the sun" one seat, David\'s sentence "before all Israel and before the sun" (2 Sam 12:12); computed) → {A(25, 4, "דבר", "ית", "כל", "רישי", "עמא", "ודון", "וקטול", "דחיב", "קטול", "קדם", "יי", "לקבל", "שמשא")} ("take all the heads of the people AND JUDGE AND KILL WHOEVER DESERVES DEATH before the LORD, opposite the sun" — the court written into the verse: the heads are the judges, the hanged are the guilty (the exam\'s Sanhedrin 35a), cut from the shelf\'s bytes); "{H(25, 4, "וישב", "חרון", "אף", "יהוה", "מישראל")}" ("and the burning anger of the LORD will turn back from Israel" — "the burning anger of the LORD" in the Torah here and at Moses\' "to add to the burning anger of the LORD against Israel" (32:14); computed) → {A(25, 4, "ויתוב", "תקוף", "רוגזא", "דיי", "מישראל")} ("and the strength of the LORD\'s anger will turn back from Israel"). The register: "and He said".')
row(25, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'MOSES TO THE JUDGES OF ISRAEL — THE OFFICE\'S FIRST NAMING: SLAY EACH HIS MEN. "{H(25, 5, "ויאמר", "משה", "אל", "שפטי", "ישראל")}" ("and Moses said to THE JUDGES OF ISRAEL" — the noun\'s first seat as an office (Deut 16:18\'s "judges and officers" and 19:18\'s "the judges" follow; Exod 12:12 and Num 33:4 "judgments" the homograph); Jethro\'s chiefs of thousands, hundreds, fifties and tens (Exod 18:21) are the exam\'s count; computed) → {A(25, 5, "ואמר", "משה", "לדיני", "ישראל")} ("and Moses said to the judges of Israel"); "{H(25, 5, "הרגו", "איש", "אנשיו", "הנצמדים", "לבעל", "פעור")}" ("slay each his men who were YOKED to Baal-peor" — "each his men" one seat; the yoke-verb\'s second seat) → {A(25, 5, "קטולו", "גבר", "גברוהי", "דאתחברו", "לבעלא", "פעור")} ("kill each his men who joined themselves to Baal-peor"). The register: "and he said".')
